{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773422635,"nonce":"dB5mCL219/WjCQHYIAcTpCBL5NU=","title":"Add notification level filtering to reduce Telegram noise","message":"## Problem\n\nTelegram gets every notification (start, resume, done, error, review rounds, etc.) which is noisy. Most of the time the user only cares about genuine questions that need human input.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd a `level` setting to notification config in WORKFLOW.md:\n\n```yaml\nnotifications:\n  - kind: telegram\n    token: $TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN\n    chat_id: $TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID\n    level: questions\n```\n\nThree levels:\n- **questions** — only @@QUESTION@@ / waiting:answer (needs human input)\n- **actions** — questions + done/accept/reject + max review rounds escalation (needs human action)\n- **all** — everything (current behavior, default for backward compat)\n\n## Implementation\n\n1. Add `level` field to `NotifierConfig` in `core/config/models.py` (default: `all`)\n2. Add `level` parameter to the `Notifier.notify()` protocol (or add a separate `notify(msg, level=...)` signature)\n3. Tag each `notifier.notify()` call site with its level:\n   - `questions`: core/qa_flow.py (line 35)\n   - `actions`: core/post_run.py (lines 44, 60, 91), core/session.py (lines 76, 102), review_orchestrator.py (escalation)\n   - `all`: everything else (auto-start, resume, review rounds, command results)\n4. `CompositeNotifier` and `TelegramNotifier` filter based on configured level\n5. `send_question()` always goes through regardless of level (it's the Q\u0026A round-trip, not just a notification)\n\n## Files to change\n\n- `core/config/models.py` — add `level` to NotifierConfig\n- `core/config/loader.py` — parse `level` from notifications config\n- `core/protocols.py` — add `level` param to notify()\n- `core/post_run.py`, `core/qa_flow.py`, `core/session.py` — tag notify calls\n- `host/watcher/` — tag notify calls in review_orchestrator, verdict_handler, command_executor, session_monitor\n- `adapters/notifiers/telegram.py`, `adapters/notifiers/webhook.py`, `adapters/notifiers/composite.py` — filter by level\n\n## Requirement\n\nREQ-008 (Notifications)","files":null}]}